Scoring discipline:
- Do not give high scores merely because the manuscript is entertaining.
- Do not give low scores merely because the manuscript is pseudo-serious or stylistically odd.
- If evidence is missing, say so directly and lower confidence.
- Reward emotional or social truth when the manuscript converts it into an argument.
- Do not reward hate, stalking, doxxing, revenge porn, explicit sexual exploitation, or actionable crime instructions, even if the prose is funny.

